[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue, on subject lines. Read the reports and it
holds three problems. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October with two of them settled. The third
is still open.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, but one of its problems is not: dates that move by one day. Track it in
<a href="https://github.com/romedina/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3">issue #3</a>.
</Callout>

## Where each problem stands

| problem | what it is | ticket | state |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | the shared parser read every date month first; day-first tenants got day and month swapped | [#1](https://github.com/romedina/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) | **fixed** · `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| `hint` | the booking-v3 form printed `MM/DD/YYYY` and read the date day first | [#2](https://github.com/romedina/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) | **won't fix** · booking-v3 form retired |
| one-day move | the date moves by one day, or differs by the viewer's place; not a swap | [#3](https://github.com/romedina/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3) | **open** · not covered by either change |

## What was merged, as the desk counts it

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The reports read as a one-day move stay counted under `parser`, where the desk filed them by
tenant, and are footnoted under the table. They are a different problem: "Invite says Tuesday 12
May. Calendar says Monday 11 May." "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday."
A day/month fix cannot move a date by one day, so the parser fix does not close them.

## Why it merged

The desk merges on subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
The same subject lines ("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong", …) came in for all three
problems, so every report landed in #4471. The intake tag guesses from the reporter's browser;
the "tagged as" column shows how often it disagrees with the tenant.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- Closed is not done: check every problem a ticket holds before you close it.
- A date that moves by one day is not a date that swaps. Read the body, not the subject.

